  "source": "https://bulletins.psu.edu/undergraduate/colleges/arts-architecture/digital-arts-media-design-bdes/",
  "notes": "Digital Art and Design Emphasis (of three: Digital Art and Design, Interactive Media and Games, Animation and Time Based Media -- Digital Art and Design chosen since it's the only track with a fully enumerated course list; the Animation track only names vague categories like 'storyboarding/illustration courses' with no codes, and would be a genuine data-ambiguity wall like Art B.A./B.F.A.'s concentrations). Greatly extended dart_catalog.json (2 -> 24 courses) and added ART 476 to art_catalog.json. Real gap fixed: ART 476 (concurrent with DART 400) requires '3 credits of ARTH', but the bulletin's own suggested plan never otherwise schedules any ARTH course -- added ARTH 111 as an explicit Semester 1 item. The three 'DART 203, 204, or 205 (select one)' pool items (Semesters 2-4) rely on the engine's tiered option ranking to naturally advance through all three distinct options, same convention as Graphic Design's repeated 'GD 300/315/320/400' pool. The 20-credit emphasis requirement is modeled with 5 literal picks from its enumerated course list (DART 403, PHOTO 202, DART 324, DART 304, DART 206 -- 18cr, 2cr short of the stated 20cr minimum since the bulletin's own per-semester Additional-Courses credit ranges didn't fully reconcile to a single value, the same kind of minor source-summarization gap hit with Landscape Architecture); the plan's broader Additional Courses pool comfortably exceeds the emphasis minimum in practice. 2026-08-27 re-verification: no separate School of Visual Arts undergraduate handbook found beyond the bulletin -- verified against the live bulletin's own Suggested Academic Plan tab HTML (DOM-extracted directly, not the summarized page). Found and fixed a real mislabel: Fourth Year Fall (Semester 7) has TWO real 'Additional Courses' cells (footnote 1) plus a separate GA-tagged Gen Ed cell, but this plan only modeled one Additional Courses cell (via the literal DART 324 emphasis pick) and left the second as a plain, unlabeled 'GEN ED' -- relabeled it to 'Additional Course for Major' (bumped 3cr->4cr to match the row's own printed '3-4' range, same convention as the other cells in this pool). Also discovered the bulletin's footnote 1 names a real, closed 60-course list for the generic 10-12cr 'in addition, select ... in consultation with faculty adviser' remainder of Additional Courses (spanning AA, ART, CMPSC, COMM, DART, GD, INART, IST, MUSIC, PHOTO, THEA) -- added all 8 previously-missing departments to `departments` and wired all 3 generic 'Additional Course for Major' slots (Semesters 2, 4, 7) to this literal list instead of leaving them fully generic/unfillable, same tiered-pool convention as Graphic Design's repeated 'GD 300/315/320/400'. The emphasis-list credit total (still 18cr from the plan's 5 literal picks, 2cr under the stated 20cr minimum) and the resulting overall Additional Courses total (still short of the bulletin's stated 30cr minimum by roughly 1-2cr depending on which end of each row's printed credit range is used) are the same kind of minor source-summarization gap documented elsewhere in this session (e.g. Landscape Architecture) -- not force-padded with invented credits. The 60-course list's own DART 206/304/403/324/PHOTO 202 (already used as this plan's 5 literal emphasis picks) and DART 495 (already a separate required Semester 5 item) were excluded from the 3 generic-pool option lists -- without this, build_full_plan() actually deadlocked (24 simulated terms, never finishing) because the engine kept trying to recommend an already-fully-consumed course code for the generic slot forever; a real engine-mechanics gotcha worth flagging for any future major reusing a literal-options-pool alongside other literal picks from the same catalog.",
